Subject: The profile records a shape table, so a contracted layout has a field list

What this does
  - The profiler writes a shape table: one `P` line per distinct shape any field
    site observed, with the prototype that shape belongs to and the ordered
    property list. A site's `shapeN=` entry carries the table index.
  - A shape's prototype is named by the prototype's own `constructor` data
    property when that holds a bytecode function -- its digest is what the unit
    binds by -- and otherwise by the well-known prototype it is, or by its
    address, which the generator refuses to contract. Only a plain data property
    is read, so no getter runs.
  - Field atoms are written by name, so a rebuilt script still matches.
  - A site takes a reference on each shape it records (at most four), and the
    dump drops them after printing. A recorded shape therefore cannot be freed
    and its address reused before the table is read, which is what makes the
    table index trustworthy.
  - `qjs_aot_layout_build` builds a contracted layout's chain: a temporary object
    of the prototype takes the fields in order through `add_property`, so the
    chain is the hashed chain any interpreter path arrives at, and one reference
    is taken on every shape of it. The shape the chain ends carries the layout id.
  - A slot index per observed shape is recorded too, as a convenience for the
    generator.

Why we need it
  A compiled body can only read a field at a constant slot if it knows the field's
  place in the layout, and no single property site knows a layout's whole field
  list. The shape table supplies it, per shape, once. Contracting the layout then
  means the offsets are facts and the body checks the contract at entry rather
  than reloading a cell offset at every access.

Functions touched
  `aot_dump_shapes` (new), `js_aot_prof_pic`, `js_aot_prof_dump`, `js_aot_digest`
  (reused), and the new `qjs_aot_layout_build`; `JSShape` gains the profiler's
  table fields.

No (the table is written only by a profiling build, and no layout is contracted
until a unit declares one).

